SUMMARY:Nutcracker: Cast B Dress Rehearsal – ACT I Cast B (Mandatory 
 – Production Week)
LOCATION:Robinson Center
DESCRIPTION:*** THIS DAY ***\nCALL TIME 6:00 PM — be checked in and bac
 kstage by then. ARRIVE BY 5:45 PM.\nOn stage: 7:00 PM–7:45 PM.\nACT I 
 Dress Run\; In Performance Costumes\, Hair and Makeup.\nMANDATORY — pr
 oduction week.\n\n*** STANDING RULES ***\nBA: Call Time is the time danc
 ers should be check-in and backstage - Arrive 15 minutes before Call Tim
 e.\nBA: Mandatory Rehearsals (1st Rehearsal\, Rehearsals after Thanksgiv
 ing and Production Week Rehearsals and Performances).\nAll Casts are cal
 led unless a cast is named.\nSUBJECT TO CHANGE — the BA master schedul
 e\, the weekly BA emails and the BA portal are the official source. Mast
 er: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1xWFCPfY5m0aK9d5dnxvALNre-6-N
 7Cl0kkw24rvm6cE/\n\n*** COSTUME / HAIR / MAKEUP — Lieutenants ***\nSol
 diers: Leiutenants — Costume (you provide): Male: Black tights\, black
  fitted t-shirt Female: Black Seamless Tights\, Black Camisole Leotard\;
  Shoes: Black Ballet Shoes\; Makeup: Light Stage Makeup\; Hair: Male: Ha
 ir out of the eyes Female: High Bun\, No Part\; Accessories (BA provides
 ): White Gloves\; Prop (BA provides): White gun\nLight Stage Makeup Inst
 ruction Sheet:\n• Powder matching skintone\n• Light brown eye shadow
  applied to the crease with an eye shadow brush\n• Dark Brown/Black ey
 eliner and black mascara. No fake lashes.\n• Blush on the cheeks (be s
 ure to apply plenty so dancer doesn’t look washed out in the stage lig
 hts)\n• Red or Dark Red lipstick\nDancers of Color may wear flesh tone
  tights and flesh tone ballet shoes.\nCostume Care Guidelines:\n• Hand
 le costume pieces with care while changing to prevent damage to delicate
  fabrics\n• Promptly notify Ballet Arkansas in the event of costume da
 mage at the point of discovery\, no matter how significant\n• Never th
 row costumes or accessories on the floor\, or hang costumes by their ela
 stic straps\n• Refrain from sitting on the floor while in costume\n•
  Do not attempt to alter\, mend\, clean\, or launder any costume or acce
 ssory\n• Never apply stage make-up while in costume and shall take gre
 at care to refrain from smudging make-up on costume during its removal\n
 • Refrain from the use of spray perfume or cologne while in costume\n
 • Never wear any garment not assigned to cast member\n• Do not handl
 e or consume food or beverage while in costume\, with the exception of w
 ater\n• Do not remove costumes from their assigned dressing rooms or f
 rom the theater\n• Remove all bobby pins used to secure head pieces an
 d wigs following their use\n• Return all headpieces to their assigned 
 bags\n• Comply fully with any and all updates to Ballet Arkansas’ wa
 rdrobe policies\n• Do not pack markers\, paints\, colored drinks or an
 ything that may damage or stain costumes.
